# Who is asked to review what.
#
# This file does nothing on its own today, and saying otherwise would be the
# kind of claim it exists to guard against. The repository has one
# collaborator, who authors every PR, and GitHub never requests review from
# an author; the `protect-main` ruleset currently sets
# `required_approving_review_count: 0` and `require_code_owner_review:
# false`. Turning this list into enforcement is a repository setting, not a
# commit: set `require_code_owner_review` on that ruleset once a second
# person exists who can satisfy it.
#
# It is written now anyway, because the moment it starts to matter - a
# second maintainer - is the moment nobody thinks to draw the distinction.
# With the list in place, broadening the catch-all is a one-line change and
# the entries under it stay where they are; without it, the natural move is
# one broad rule and no separation at all.
#
# The criterion below: paths where a change can weaken a guarantee without
# touching product code. Last match wins, so the specific paths come after
# the catch-all.

*                                       @takashi-matsuyama

# --- What CI enforces ------------------------------------------------------

# What runs, with what permissions, and which checks gate a merge.
/.github/workflows/                     @takashi-matsuyama

# Who Dependabot may bump and how: the update path for every pinned
# third-party action.
/.github/dependabot.yml                 @takashi-matsuyama

# --- What CI is told to ignore ---------------------------------------------
# The two files whose entire purpose is to be read rather than trusted. Each
# can stop a required check from failing on a real finding, silently, and
# each covers one of the two blocking scans.

/.github/osv-scanner-exceptions.toml    @takashi-matsuyama
/.gitleaks.toml                         @takashi-matsuyama

# --- What gets scanned, built and published --------------------------------

# Builds the trees the blocking dependency scan runs against; can narrow
# what is scanned without touching the scanner.
/scripts/derive-consumer-manifests.mjs  @takashi-matsuyama

# The published container image: base layer, what is copied in, what runs.
/Dockerfile                             @takashi-matsuyama

# --- What we promise -------------------------------------------------------

# The disclosure contract: where a reporter is told to go, and what they are
# told to expect.
/SECURITY.md                            @takashi-matsuyama
